# VM short-circuit + negative (legacy `test/vm/99_short_circuit`, `15_nested_mutation`)

`out-of-bounds` strengthens the legacy any-`Err` weak oracle with an
independently reviewed strong diagnostic (T-01 probe evidence: the VM traps
with `RuntimeError("Array index 10 out of bounds …")`); the legacy suite
keeps its original weak assertion untouched.

```test-case
case {
  schema: "autolang.case/1"
  id: "lang.shortcircuit.and-or"
  tags: ["pilot", "vm", "short-circuit"]
  source: { file: "vm/99_short_circuit/001_and_or_short_circuit/and_or_short_circuit.at", syntax: "auto", path: "main.at" }
  entry: { mode: "program" }
  checks: [
    { id: "vm", adapter: "avm", action: "run",
      expect: { completion: "success", stdout: { text: "A: 0\nB else\nC else\nSIDE\nD: 1\nE taken\nSIDE\nSIDE\nSIDE\nF: 4\nSIDE\nG: 1\nH: false true\nI norm-false\n", compare: "bytes" } } }
  ]
}
```

